# Toolchain pins for the Dev Platform envs (ghc_*_dp) ONLY.
#
# This file is read exclusively by the QA framework's DP flow, which pushes each
# entry as a repo-level env var before the scan. Classic envs (ghc_dev,
# ghc_staging, ghe) never read it, so their currently-green runs are unaffected.
#
# WHY: on DP the php/composer toolchain is provisioned from MEND_SCA_VERSIONING_*
# env vars, which are normally derived from .whitesource -> scanSettings.versioning.
# symfony's .whitesource carries no versioning block, so the DP env-var step logged
# "Derived 0 allowed entries from .whitesource", no toolchain was installed, and the
# php resolver produced nothing -- the scan reported RESOLUTION:3 (html/archive only),
# no VERSIONING step, 6 direct / 0 transitive, and totalFail:{} with no partialScanError.
# The probes that DO resolve on DP all carry a versioning pin and show a VERSIONING step.
#
# composer.json requires php >=8.4.1. php 8.4 + composer 2.8 are known installable on
# this lane -- composer-version-matrix-php84-composer28-probe pins exactly that pair
# and passes on ghc_staging_dp.
#
# Pinning here rather than in .whitesource is deliberate: .whitesource IS read by the
# classic envs, so putting the pin there would change three green lanes to fix one.
MEND_SCA_VERSIONING_PHP=8.4
MEND_SCA_VERSIONING_COMPOSER=2.8
